of Dandaka, those best of the twice-born ones, said to us-Be you gracious to us.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.369,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0dac6ee7e7024b144b2fb6da046189330e16a8e2228f4632fff9060600516070","compact":"9b2f9c99a2a0dc73644ccbcc2ccc758c2d4774eefa6668d4326287d47667644b","nasal":"8ede406bd3ca0a49a06b4192cb6b0467d794c469b35a3b64ab81b991caae1720"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":7,"english":"Always dwelling in the forest, subsisting on fruits and roots, they on account of Rākṣasas of cruel deeds do not, O timid attain ease. These ascetics are devoured by terrible Rākṣasas living on human flesh. Being eaten up (by the Rākşasas), the anchorites living in the forest of Dandaka, those best of the twice-born ones, said to us-Be you gracious to us.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90128b071bfeab81252ccd492ac4d7352463563eb4a71adf5db78b56bdeee0ee","compact":"20656a4767344d6bb088e49f18dd3f7c71510ec054066fdaea2a51404f72c6ff","nasal":"524f89ea4dfb06930121a2b0628aea7633256dc1e6e8631def058550f444c656"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":8,"english":"Hearing those words of theirs which fell from their lips, I, resolving to act in accordance with their request, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0412df5b7d01b71293108adf53a5145250104e5464abd42e15c385a2b5400195","compact":"6803e34b0b24065fc1c5a50443704f84ea9d1b4222ca5aca2127f5956ff8669b","nasal":"6803e34b0b24065fc1c5a50443704f84ea9d1b4222ca5aca2127f5956ff8669b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":9,"english":"'Be you propitious.' This is surpassing shame to me that such Vipras who themselves are worthy of being sought, seek me. What shall I do? I said this in the presence of those twiceborn ones.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.832,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da7a83145198606ba81a7522cba9734080c0dba784f945aa3cb15dd757d5605f","compact":"b82f340772404ea3f59e672ff889d70a397f2094bd656bf3fc657bdd45709843","nasal":"9f5065680525b55a97512b227fc93612bdbdee7feec530b7ddedaf429f79621f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":10,"english":"Thereat all those that had come, said, We have been, O Rāma, immensely harassed in the forest of Dandaka by Räkşasas wearing shapes at will. Do you deliver us.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.608,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b6065ae21a501a2412c22d7859d69487e33861c36799ba50b9f437e1eac79ed","compact":"ec1e8b28edb83e6053a624b2b6b38742ee9f7307cb3a270aed82ebb04a4d2173","nasal":"2a605568333e7999c707aa8b6763d1a73e608aef8bf9bd078bd0b3cbd9dcf675"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":11,"english":"O sinless one! These irrepressible Rākṣasas living on human flesh vanquish us at the time of Homa, and on the occasions of Parvas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e05d324ddcb48ab784f549c4332523e3db9c3efb9bd7321f1212d520c38bed9","compact":"aa2942e37a97cdb2c18b6a306fb8fa0ae38928df73207b32cec4ccd992395a17","nasal":"c3fcc78bb2dc4831982c0cba48ab89db8b9d05d02e7012fdfae817c0237d5269"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":12,"english":"Of the saints and ascetics afflicted by the Rākşasas, who are on the search for their refuge, you are our best refuge. sore","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f06ad77f513dcd70b0a09cad3fb23745e5100c37c0e183b1f03cfa892913b2aa","compact":"4faa022d24dc66807b21236e6bcfa9911ece7b9dd9fcea93e68b5184e7b03b09","nasal":"a963bfe7412e9020a7facfa6f931855ae0736c536b0aea3e781f346b67a66e63"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":13,"english":"We can by virtue of the energy of our asceticism easily destroy the rangers of the night; but we are loath to lose our asceticism earned in a long time. O Rāghava our austerities are constantly disturbed, and we can hardly perform thein.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89e495386140737267bb68fc3ed6ed3f7ef3159b1274b3fdcc9b1527d9e893b6","compact":"06426d1c9f2ef76cd3161c660a6e555b3258a4bbeaa0c6a2126f558133c16b2e","nasal":"c084ade598163a248730f8662ca51ded3808ce729ad2ad493ef2f54d38362e42"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":14,"english":"We can by virtue of the energy of our asceticism easily destroy the rangers of the night; but we are loath to lose our asceticism earned in a long time. O Rāghava our austerities are constantly disturbed, and we can hardly perform thein. Therefore, although afflicted and devoured by the Rākşasas dwelling in the forest of Dandaka, we do not cast our curse on them. You along with your brother are our protector: you are our master in this forest.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.484,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-11","DUTT-3-10-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"701dbcb94fba800d357dc4d6e7f6391f4c79967c8f12b3d88d2bfd4ef1f009c0","compact":"8a9536666fc630873972284106e5d9f2457cc300206f21e0da0b0a58f0c1265b","nasal":"30f91e68f50bac341795d15da50548814b96b5e1bc21b2cd5113a06631803dd7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":15,"english":"Therefore, although afflicted and devoured by the Rākşasas dwelling in the forest of Dandaka, we do not cast our curse on them. You along with your brother are our protector: you are our master in this forest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.786,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25ae108fb1ff29e320fd9a3482d3a4e481ccc402cd51932c33ee70441d830631","compact":"1dc23ca7e4de5cec07e6db29d0c0faa35736c7ee32c515f5718a7cc614b7957e","nasal":"f8e49ab1db844da161f0e3d8a63ecd96bc8a2dba24d3f6b89402ef3ad33da6e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":16,"english":"Having heard these words, I promised my perfect protection to the saints in the forest of Dandaka, O daughter of Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca515fb0a5648471c5dabc71d8beefc16313284405bbbbc79b9ae8fe29a997e5","compact":"60b230bec5346080b32c01acf4b14b9b4cfad7f5e860d88d15e92cfa57aeb47f","nasal":"2cebd2cf5ca363df77322be19335b8ab75333d3ac47b5663c4135cb09e4e96a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":17,"english":"Having promised, I living cannot violate my vow concerning the ascetics; verily truth is ever dear to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a6ba194ffab83738c4844725bb5a1678dca1635635a7ac807246398b17f03a2","compact":"9f960ed32aca0a9542797484b621d27602e8c24cad59dcf2c1577b07cfff76d1","nasal":"4eb6eb49a1664128b06325085b35314780597b403ac4eae7a3872c2bb36e081e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":18,"english":"I had rather renounce my life, or you, O Sītā, along with Lakşmaņa-but by no means my promise made, especially to Brahmanas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-10-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3009018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cde3a3586b59c52a0825a48a24bdbdfb10d8050fd8d03c03426e704fa9aa923d","compact":"88f89a069fa0db6d8a7bbd122c2979f8d70dadafffc50c1129b895b404575678","nasal":"88f89a069fa0db6d8a7bbd122c2979f8d70dadafffc50c1129b895b404575678"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-9-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":9,"verse":19,"english":"O Videha's daughter, the protection of the saints is incumbent on me even without any representation, and what (shall I say) when I have promised the same?","alignment":{"ty